    "h-opplate": "Convolutions, pooling and matmuls cannot be folded into scalar neurons (a 3×3, 64→64 convolution over a 256×256 feature map is hundreds of millions of edges), so in the viewport each one is a <b>plate</b>: the texture is its largest parameter tensor (blue = positive, red = negative, brighter = larger magnitude; integer parameters use a cyan ramp) and the border colour comes from the operator type.",
    "h-oppick": "Operator nodes and neurons are bridged by exactly one thing: the <b>landing</b> — which neurons the output is written into, one element per neuron, so the counts must match. Click a plate to select it; click empty space to deselect.",
    "h-opsim": "Operator nodes take part in <b>compiling</b> only; during a simulation the signal stops as soon as it reaches one (a convolution has no scalar value to threshold against). The simulation panel says the same thing.",

